{"content":[{"c":["HATRED"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Intense feeling of aversion or enmity, which could prompt a person to loathe someone or something, or even to seek revenge for having been wronged. The Scriptures forbid people to hate others (",{"href":"?bref=Lev.19.17-18","r":"Lev.19.17-18","rawR":"Lev.19.17-18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Lev.19.17-18","value":"Lev.19.17-18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lv 19:17-18"},") because it leads to sin. Indeed, hatred itself is considered murder (",{"href":"?bref=1Jn.3.15","r":"1Jn.3.15","rawR":"1Jn.3.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Jn.3.15","value":"1Jn.3.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Jn 3:15"},"). We are called upon to let God, the holy one, avenge all wrongs (",{"href":"?bref=Pr.20.22","r":"Pr.20.22","rawR":"Pr.20.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Pr.20.22","value":"Pr.20.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Prv 20:22"},"), and we are commanded by Jesus to love our enemies (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.5.43-44","r":"Matt.5.43-44","rawR":"Matt.5.43-44","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.5.43-44","value":"Matt.5.43-44"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 5:43-44"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["Not all aspects of hatred are sinful. The Scriptures tell us that God hates evil (",{"href":"?bref=Pr.6.16-19","r":"Pr.6.16-19","rawR":"Pr.6.16-19","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Pr.6.16-19","value":"Pr.6.16-19"}],"t":"ref","v":"Prv 6:16-19"},") and evil people (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.5.5","r":"Ps.5.5","rawR":"Ps.5.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.5.5","value":"Ps.5.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 5:5"},"). The Scripture also has expressions such as “Jacob have I loved; Esau I have hated” (",{"href":"?bref=Mal.1.2-3","r":"Mal.1.2-3","rawR":"Mal.1.2-3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mal.1.2-3","value":"Mal.1.2-3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mal 1:2-3"},"). This means that God elected Jacob and not Esau to be the progenitor of the chosen Jewish race. In similar fashion, would-be Christians are challenged by Jesus to hate their lives and earthly relationships if they want to follow him (",{"href":"?bref=Luke.14.26","r":"Luke.14.26","rawR":"Luke.14.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.14.26","value":"Luke.14.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 14:26"},"). This means that they must choose Jesus above all else."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Hatred","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Lv 19:17-18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Lev.19.17-18","rawQueryValue":"Lev.19.17-18","sourceRefExact":"Lev.19.17-18"},{"anchorText":"1 Jn 3:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Jn.3.15","rawQueryValue":"1Jn.3.15","sourceRefExact":"1Jn.3.15"},{"anchorText":"Prv 20:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Pr.20.22","rawQueryValue":"Pr.20.22","sourceRefExact":"Pr.20.22"},{"anchorText":"Mt 5:43-44","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.5.43-44","rawQueryValue":"Matt.5.43-44","sourceRefExact":"Matt.5.43-44"},{"anchorText":"Prv 6:16-19","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Pr.6.16-19","rawQueryValue":"Pr.6.16-19","sourceRefExact":"Pr.6.16-19"},{"anchorText":"Ps 5:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.5.5","rawQueryValue":"Ps.5.5","sourceRefExact":"Ps.5.5"},{"anchorText":"Mal 1:2-3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Mal.1.2-3","rawQueryValue":"Mal.1.2-3","sourceRefExact":"Mal.1.2-3"},{"anchorText":"Lk 14:26","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Luke.14.26","rawQueryValue":"Luke.14.26","sourceRefExact":"Luke.14.26"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"3a4614c6cee9ee9982ef64bde808e7e0f17eb370ea8b355138679633f3652031","sourceItemName":"Hatred","sourceItemOrder":161,"sourceMember":"Articles/H.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Hatred","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Hatred","title":"Hatred","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}